From 17df8615f032d6d81ecde21eea08c42a56778c72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lei Wen <lei.wen@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2014 09:53:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] platform/x86: Add Intel generic MCU control interface

We define three tty channels along with sysfs nodes for userspace communicate
with MCU side. Those three tty interfaces are as:
/dev/ttymcu0:
  This channel services as user customized message service.
  User need to define their own format in both IA and MCU sides.
/dev/ttymcu1:
  This channel services as interface to get MCU side trace.
/dev/ttymcu2:
  This channel services as interface for GDB to hook with.

Those three sysfs nodes are as:
/sys/devices/platform/intel_mcu/control
  It is served as load the MCU application.
/sys/devices/platform/intel_mcu/fw_version
  It is served as read out application version.
/sys/devices/platform/intel_mcu/log_level
  It is served as set and read app log level.

